 "details": {
  "title": "Isn’t It Romantic",
  "lead": "The chorus for trumpet in D (E for the trumpet), concert A3 to E5, set on the bars of the Fret Finder guitar arrangement, which follows Rod Stewart’s record four semitones lower, about 105 and swung: the chorus, the second chorus, the second half again after his short interlude, and the last line three times. Rod starts the title an eighth late on C♯, and the line does too. The lead sheet has no verse, so over the free verse the trumpet plays a short line of its own, waits, and leads in. There is a breath before each pickup.",
  "facts": [
   [
    "Song",
    "Richard Rodgers and Lorenz Hart (1932)"
   ],
   [
    "Line",
    "The chorus from the lead sheet on the Fret Finder page’s chords; the verse line, the interlude fill and the tag are our own"
   ],
   [
    "Key",
    "D major concert (E for the trumpet), four semitones below Rod Stewart’s record"
   ],
   [
    "Form",
    "Verse, chorus, second chorus, interlude, the second half again, tag"
   ],
   [
    "Plays with",
    "The guitar track on the Fret Finder page (iir-guitar.mp3), 3:49"
   ],
   [
